        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): add handshakeTimeout to probe WebSocket",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes. I reviewed and understand the change.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Signal container REST probe WebSocket creates `new WebSocket()` without `handshakeTimeout`. The production receiver socket at line 380 already sets `handshakeTimeout: WS_HANDSHAKE_MS` (30 s) — only the probe socket was missed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd `handshakeTimeout: WS_HANDSHAKE_MS` (30 s) to the probe WebSocket, using the same constant already defined and already applied to the receiver socket. This is the narrowest possible fix — one line, reusing existing infrastructure.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSignal container health probes now fail within 30 seconds on a stalled WebSocket upgrade instead of hanging indefinitely.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n\n- `signal/src/client-container.test.ts`: **65/65 passed**.\n- `expect(wsMockState.options).toEqual([{ maxPayload: 1048576, handshakeTimeout: 30_000 }])` — verifies the constant reaches the constructor.\n\n### ws library contract proof\n\n```json\n{\"handshakeTimeout_ms\":2000,\"error\":\"Opening handshake has timed out\",\"elapsed_ms\":2011,\"result\":\"TIMED_OUT\"}\n{\"handshakeTimeout_ms\":30000,\"error\":\"aborted after 2s\",\"elapsed_ms\":2013,\"result\":\"ABORTED_EARLY_(still_waiting_at_30s_deadline)\"}\n```\n\nThe production value (30 s) is not firing early (still waiting at 2 s). Smaller values fire on time (2 s → 2011 ms). The pre-fix default (0) waits indefinitely.\n\nThe parameter flow: **OpenClaw probe → `new WebSocket(url, { handshakeTimeout: WS_HANDSHAKE_MS })` → ws library enforces deadline**. The unit test verifies the parameter reaches the constructor; this proof verifies the ws library enforces it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
